{"type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn6le02ob01re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn6le02ob01re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn6le02ob01re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"image": "engenn6le02ob01re2img01.jpg", "text": "Born in 1961, Lady Diana Spencer had a fairly normal upbringing out of the public eye.\nHer quiet life did nothing to prepare her for the fame and glamor that being a British princess brought with it. When Prince Charles met Diana, she was a kindergarten teacher in London. In a short time, the shy teenager became one of most photographed people in the world. Soon she won the hearts of the British people with her timid smiles and quiet natural beauty. Her fairytale royal wedding to Prince Charles in 1981 was watched with excitement by people around the world.", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"image": "engenn6le02ob01re2img02.jpg", "text": "Naturally, Diana was nervous to be in public at first, but she quickly changed, becoming the relaxed, charming royal many would come to love. She immediately became interested in charities and important causes, drawing public focus. She raised awareness of how many people suffered by visiting the homeless, lepers, and victims of AIDS. She was open and compassionate prompting others to be as well. She strongly campaigned against the use of landmines and so many countries banned their use. Diana's name was constantly found in newspaper headlines.", "time": "34000", "id": 2}, {"image": "engenn6le02ob01re2img03.jpg", "text": "Sadly, the biggest headline of all marked her sudden death at 36. When he spoke at Diana's funeral, British Prime Minister Tony Blair referred to her as the \"People's Princess\". However, her adoring public simply called her the \"Queen of Hearts\".", "time": "63000", "i